e=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 106, "status": 200, "title": "GM-Backed Sodium-Ion Batteries Target 20% Lower Costs for Grid Energy Storage – NaturalNews.com", "unwound_url": "https://naturalnews.com/2026-10-28-sodium-ion-batteries-target-lower-costs-storage.html", "url": "https://t.co/DC92vM46Xw"}]}, "id": "2115897953835778163", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "GM-Backed Sodium-Ion Batteries Target 20% Lower Costs for Grid Energy Storage   – https://t.co/lzaEQP7nyK https://t.co/DC92vM46Xw", "url": "https://x.com/MinPeacefulPoet/status/2115897953835778163"}, {"author_id": "2409164347", "created_at": "2026-10-28T11:46:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115409794354106555"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 101, "start": 87, "tag": "energystorage"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/JKwICsExYs", "end": 125, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/energystoragenw/status/2115409794354106555/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115409792391127040", "start": 102, "url": "https://t.co/JKwICsExYs"}]}, "id": "2115409794354106555", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 240, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Data centres could drive sodium-ion, LDES adoption in Europe – analyst dlvr.​it/TW5KYY #energystorage https://t.co/JKwICsExYs", "url": "https://x.com/energystoragenw/status/2115409794354106555"}, {"author_id": "1658462217845768199", "created_at": "2026-10-29T09:14:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115733892133179524"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 133, "start": 127, "tag": "China"}, {"end": 137, "start": 134, "tag": "EV"}], "urls": [{"description": "CATL and Germany's Intilion signed an agreement to deploy 3 GWh of sodium-ion storage across German-speaking markets over five years, the battery maker said.", "display_url": "chinaindustryintel.com/catl-takes-its…", "end": 161, "expanded_url": "https://chinaindustryintel.com/catl-takes-its-sodium-ion-storage-to-europe-in-a-3-gwh-deal/", "images": [{"height": 560, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115733898839867392/IYIOmjQn?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 960}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115733898839867392/IYIOmjQn?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 138, "status": 200, "title": "CATL Takes Its Sodium-Ion Storage to Europe in a 3 GWh Deal", "unwound_url": "https://chinaindustryintel.com/catl-takes-its-sodium-ion-storage-to-europe-in-a-3-gwh-deal/", "url": "https://t.co/NV1uVAQmEu"}]}, "id": "2115733892133179524", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "No lithium needed: CATL's 3 GWh sodium-ion deal brings batteries rated for 15,000+ cycles to Germany, Switzerland and Austria. #China #EV\nhttps://t.co/NV1uVAQmEu", "url": "https://x.com/cii_Kenjitanaka/status/2115733892133179524"}, {"author_id": "3591710966", "created_at": "2026-10-29T04:05:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115656208900034951"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 19, "start": 2, "tag": "HighlyCitedPaper"}, {"end": 148, "start": 131, "tag": "SodiumIonBattery"}, {"end": 176, "start": 149, "tag": "AcceleratedRateCalorimetry"}, {"end": 191, "start": 177, "tag": "SafetyTesting"}, {"end": 208, "start": 192, "tag": "CommercialCells"}, {"end": 223, "start": 210, "tag": "mdpienergies"}, {"end": 235, "start": 224, "tag": "openaccess"}], "urls": [{"description": "Herein, we investigate the performance and safety of four of the early-stage, commercial Na-ion batteries available in 2024, representing the most popular cathode types across research and commercialization: polyanion (Na-VPF), layered metal oxide (Na-NMF), and a Prussian blue analog (Na-tmCN). The cells deliver a wide range of energy density with Na-tmCN delivering the least (23 Wh/kg) and Na-NMF delivering the most (127 Wh/kg). The Na-VPF cell was in between (47 Wg/kg). Capacity retention under specified cycling conditions and with periodic 0 V excursions was the most robust for the Na-tmCN cells in both cases. Accelerating rate calorimetry (ARC) and nail penetration testing finds that Na-NMF cells do undergo thermal runaway in response to abuse, while the Na-VPF and Na-tmCN exhibit only low self-heating rates (<1 °C/min). During these safety tests, all cells exhibited off-gassing, so we conducted in-line FTIR equipped with a heated gas cell to detect CO, CO2, CH4, toxic acid gases (", "display_url": "brnw.ch/21x6KcO", "end": 128, "expanded_url": "https://brnw.ch/21x6KcO", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115656220816076800/r2bbdfTu?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115656220816076800/r2bbdfTu?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 105, "status": 200, "title": "First Look at Safety and Performance Evaluation of Commercial Sodium-Ion Batteries", "unwound_url": "https://www.mdpi.com/1996-1073/18/3/661?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social_journ&utm_campaign=energies", "url": "https://t.co/A2kkaC66IC"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/EFLTLhacq1", "end": 259, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/energies_mdpi/status/2115656208900034951/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115656205691502592", "start": 236, "url": "https://t.co/EFLTLhacq1"}]}, "id": "2115656208900034951", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 71, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "✨ #HighlyCitedPaper First Look at Safety and Performance Evaluation of Commercial Sodium-Ion Batteries\n👉 https://t.co/A2kkaC66IC \n\n#SodiumIonBattery #AcceleratedRateCalorimetry #SafetyTesting #CommercialCells\n\n#mdpienergies #openaccess https://t.co/EFLTLhacq1", "url": "https://x.com/energies_mdpi/status/2115656208900034951"}, {"author_id": "1602182754883571719", "created_at": "2026-10-28T05:32: